{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":75116,"duration_api_ms":74797,"num_turns":3,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4932a82c-fc06-42b4-b5a4-684ebeaa84da","total_cost_usd":0.23383335,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19885,"cache_read_input_tokens":72057,"output_tokens":713,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19885,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":713,"cacheReadInputTokens":72057,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19885,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.17815475,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":37,"outputTokens":2748,"cacheReadInputTokens":154716,"cacheCreationInputTokens":21144,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.05567860000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Amendment fr-2 identifies a genuine test correctness issue: the test helper uses hardcoded approximate constants (2.497, 4.118) while the implementation derives more precise values from molar masses (2.49730..., 4.11796...), producing a ~3.27e-4 discrepancy that far exceeds the 1e-9 tolerance. This is a real defect that should be fixed — either by updating the test constants to match the implementation's molar-mass-derived values, or by relaxing the tolerance. The molar-mass-based implementation is chemically more accurate, so updating the test is the right path.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-ac995bdf","decision":"accept","rationale":"The amendment correctly identifies a real test defect. The test's expected_gh_d helper uses rounded constants (2.497, 4.118) that don't match the implementation's molar-mass-derived constants (100.0869/40.078 ≈ 2.49730, 100.0869/24.305 ≈ 4.11796), causing a ~3.27e-4 discrepancy against a 1e-9 tolerance. This is not a flaky or edge-case issue — the test will deterministically fail. The fix should update the test helper to use the same molar-mass-based constants as the implementation (which is chemically more precise), not loosen the tolerance to paper over the mismatch. Even though this is pre-existing and unrelated to the CO2 changes, it is a real broken test on the branch that warrants fixing."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"bb740e62-1f58-4f79-bb7a-1bf77a0f73eb"}
